Database Migration kya hai?

Database migration ka matlab hai database ki structure (schema) mein changes ko manage aur track karna.

Matlab agar aap production app chalate ho aur aapko naye columns add karne hain,
tables change karne hain, constraints lagani hain → to manually database update karna risky hota hai.
Isliye hum migration tools use karte hain jo ye changes step by step track karte hain
aur sab environments (dev, test, prod) mein same changes apply kar dete hain.

Example situation

Pehle aapke paas table hai:

CREATE TABLE users (id INT PRIMARY KEY, name VARCHAR(100));


Ab requirement aayi ke email column bhi add karna hai.
Agar aap manually SQL chalate ho to sab developers ko batana padega.
Lekin agar aap migration script banao to wo automatically sab environments mein run ho jayega.

ALTER TABLE users ADD email VARCHAR(100);

Java world mein famous migration tools

Flyway (zyada simple aur commonly use hota hai)

SQL scripts ya Java-based migrations likh sakte ho.

Files ka naming convention hota hai like:
V1__create_users.sql, V2__add_email_to_users.sql

Liquibase

Thoda advanced hai, XML, YAML, JSON aur SQL sab support karta hai.

Zyada complex migrations ke liye use hota hai.

Migration ka faida

Sab developers ka database schema same rehta hai.

Manual SQL run karne ki zarurat nahi.

Version control system ke through track hota hai (git mein scripts save hote hain).

Deployment easy aur safe hoti hai.

Roman Urdu Summary:

Database migration ka matlab hai ke database schema ke changes ko step by step scripts ki form mein track
 karna aur automatic apply karna, taake dev, test, aur production sab jagah database ek jaisa ho.
Spring Boot projects mein mostly Flyway ya Liquibase use hota hai.